# Auto commit and push

After finishing a task that changes tracked files in this repo, **commit and push automatically**. Do not wait for the user to say "commit" or "push".

## When to commit and push

- Docs, scripts, rules, skills, builder JSON, or changelogs were edited as part of the completed task
- The work is in a good state

## When not to commit

- No tracked-file changes (only pristine/cache/workspace bins or other gitignored paths)
- The user explicitly said not to commit in this turn
- A commit hook failed — fix and create a **new** commit
- Files likely contain secrets — warn instead

Never commit `.bin` / `.cue` under `pristine/`, `cache/`, or legacy `workspace/`.

## How

1. `git status` / `git diff`
2. Stage relevant tracked files
3. Concise message (why, not file list)
4. Commit without Cursor trailers (see `no-cursor-commit-trailers.mdc`)
5. `git push` (no force; no skip-hooks; do not update git config)

